// The state bootstrap is deliberately a resource-free ordering anchor.
//
// The shared deployment shell admits exactly one DeploymentStateLocation
// from authenticated deployment metadata before this definition is
// evaluated. It validates the local/S3 locator and prepares the envelope,
// infrastructure, runtime, and operation-lock stores from that one value, so
// reproducing the locator in ECS configuration would create a second source
// of truth that could drift from the stores already in use.
//
// For S3, the bucket is a primordial, operator-owned prerequisite. Ambient
// AWS credentials must supply prefix-scoped object access; the recorded
// locator carries no credentials. Tokeira's state layer supplies encryption
// and conditional-write/CAS semantics. ECS must not
// create the bucket or take ownership of its public-access, versioning,
// policy, lifecycle, or deletion controls. For local state, the shared layer
// keeps every document under the deployment directory. This empty module
// remains the graph's unique dependency-free root so all provider work is
// still ordered after state admission.

use platform::Ecs;

pub fn define(_d: Deployment, _cfg: Ecs, _cx: Context, _remote_state: Module) {}
